{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528314-battle-scars","id":528314,"title":"Battle Scars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-25T18:22:03-07:00","id":528314,"title":"Battle Scars","content":"Is there a method of healing battle scars on a garou that have been around for a while? And I am talking more like missing limbs and not just cosmetic scarring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:42:36-07:00","id":528518,"title":"","content":"Beyond either &quot;Spirit quest for a very potent spirit of healing,&quot; or using something like Firebringer to make a Gift out of healing powers from other supernaturals that can regenerate limbs and the like (ex: A mage's Life effect at high enough level), I don't recall something for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T00:45:29-07:00","id":528625,"title":"","content":"I haven't heard how you heal them just how to get them. It seems that their is major renown for having them so I suspect the opposite is true to remove them. I'd imagine it was possible but would be frowned upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T01:03:35-07:00","id":528631,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on the tribe, loose an arm in battle as a Get you win some major points, get the arm back they will probability correct the &quot;mistake&quot; because loss of the arm was Fenris's will. Now say the children of Gaia or glasswalkers that might be a different story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T01:31:13-07:00","id":528638,"title":"","content":"Anyone with the Mother's Touch Gift (and really... how do you have a PC pack without at least one person that takes that?) can opt to heal a Battle Scar if the Gift if used in the same scene as the Battle Scar was inflicted. Though it can be a tough balance as the ST to describe the injuries so the players know the risks. Some Battle Scars are trivial and are well worth the Glory so you don't want them healed; while others can seriously impede a character.<br /> <br /> Though Dwight's post did remind me of an option I skipped for some battle scars:<br /> <br /> Fetishes. While most frequently cyber-implants and the Glasswalkers (if they even wait for you to lose the body part...), there are non-technological mythical objects that could inspire Fetishes that could replace a lost body part. A Fianna might craft a silver hand/arm in the style of Nuada (actually this might be in one of the books already...), while a Black Fury might make a Fetish eyeball that allows a blind person to see ala the Graeae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T03:44:16-07:00","id":528691,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I have a CoG PC who is looking to heal his arm and his Fenrir packmate's. His theory is just a trip to the CoG home realm should do it, but I've found no evidence and it sounds way too easy for any battle scar to exist...toss in the bears don't even seem to have a system for it.<br /> <br /> As for Fianna and Nuada's silver arm, yea it was in the first tribe book....they stated even with that he was still not allowed to have a position of power and had to step down which led to the second battle of Tara. You'd think after that they wouldn't be AS bad with their metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T03:49:27-07:00","id":528694,"title":"","content":"I remember there are rules for fetish scars and I once had a player get one. He was very happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T08:40:28-07:00","id":528796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cptmachine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/528314-battle-scars?p=528694#post528694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember there are rules for fetish scars and I once had a player get one. He was very happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fetish scars aren't the same thing as battle scars at all. One is carefully and ritually made (just look at human scarification in some real-life cultures) and then imbued with a spirit the same way any other fetish is imbued with a spirit. The other is gained from no holds barred combat with the Enemy. It's certainly possible to turn a battle scar into a fetish scar, but it's rare. I do remember one Garou from Rage Across the Amazon who lost his arm in combat (one hell of a battle scar)...and then had his amputated arm turned into a fetish club that did aggravated damage. I wouldn't call that arm-club a fetish scar, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T03:30:14-07:00","id":529735,"title":"","content":"The Stargazers have their Yoga rites, the highest level or second to highest, can over time heal Battle Scars. But besides that, there is only the spirit quest as a regular means to fully heal.<br /> <br /> Adjusting to the disadvantages a Battle Scar brings with it is another thing. Cyberimplants aren't for everyone, not even every Glasswalker. But a garou with an open skull or something like that, better wear a hat when he goes into a populated area. Such actions probably don't cause for renown loss.<br /> <br /> Gets have a gift that allows for lost limbs to be replaced by fully functional epherma prosthetics for the duration of a combat. It's athro, iirc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T14:39:21-07:00","id":530327,"title":"","content":"I think I remember some weird totem (Polar Bear?) giving the ability to either regrow or reattach severed limbs, but I'm not sure what the restrictions there are. Legendary spiritual quest and a renown loss seems otherwise par for the course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T20:02:53-07:00","id":530568,"title":"","content":"Snag is...while polar bear can allow for severed limbs to be regenerated...it's non-agg caused only it seems (W20 RatW page 121). If I tie them to the Arctic would that be seen as a good signing bonus? A 1 time heal for old battle scars (regrow limbs that have been missing for years)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 05-27-2015, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:47:52-07:00","id":659928,"title":"","content":"I would say it could be possible. Like others above I'd say it would require a quest for a powerful spirit of healing of somekind and gaining it's favor (chiminage).<br /> <br /> I would also say the character loses any renown they gained and some more. They have potentially extended their own life and efficiency in battle but at the cost of intentionally and willingly undoing the mark that brought them Glory in an act of personal valor. In essence they are undoing something that the Garou nation hold in high regard and evidence of the Garou's might. &quot;I've got an arm off...but it's just a flesh wound. Let's go make sure the Wyrm chokes on it...or if it needs another to finish the job!&quot; Valor, Glory, Bravery, inspirarion these are things a Battle scar proves you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T10:20:06-07:00","id":660851,"title":"","content":"You can always go to the flux realm and attempt to get yourself turned into a rutabaga... or grow your arm back, if you want to be dull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T14:19:15-07:00","id":661069,"title":"","content":"I'm now imagining a werewolf whose head is surrounded by a mane of giant flower petals saying &quot;Yeah, I wouldn't recommend it...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T03:48:14-07:00","id":661756,"title":"","content":"...just like Daffy Duck in that episode of chaos and breaking the fourth wall with the artist. :-)<br /> <br /> Talking of Battle scars, and hopefully not derailing too.much from the original post...does anyone have examples of additional scars and permanent wounds for characters beyond the book?<br /> <br /> I have a few characters in play and the scars have started to get a bit...samey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}